 # queue-lost-retry
 
 A compact stateful single-job queue project. Run `npm test` with Node 24 or newer.
+
+The queue exposes ready and leased jobs through `snapshot()`. `work(q, send)`
+takes at most one ready job and calls `send(job)` when work is available:
+
+- A truthy send result acknowledges the job. The worker returns its ID in
+  `sent`, and the job is removed without leaving a lease.
+- A falsy send result retries the job with its ID and payload intact. The ID is
+  returned in `retried`, the job is ready again, and unrelated ready jobs are
+  preserved.
+- A later successful call can consume the retried job.
+- An empty queue returns `{sent: [], retried: []}` and does not call `send`.
+
+The regression suite covers each of these independent flows, including the
+observable ready and leased state before and after processing.
